      "side": 1,
      "message": "Wondering: maybe instead of allowing the host to set IRTE to an _arbitrary_ value (via these opaque irte_lo \u0026 irte_hi fields) and just validating the PDA bits, we should do it similarly to how we do it in the hypercalls for setting context and PASID entries, i.e. require the host to explicitly specify the values of the needed fields?\n\nSo that pKVM can make sure that the rest of the fields are set to sane default values (e.g. at least that the Reserved bits are set to 0, as the VT-d spec requires), plus possibly do extra validation of other fields if needed.",
      "revId": "bc1442c6fa12200fc157ea252081aa5492db688d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
