      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was thinking it might not be necessary as we let the host manage the interrupts  and we validate the Posted Descriptor address just to make sure that protected memory is not tampered with. For context and pasid entries we were basically validating fields to make sure the host is not able to configure DMA such that device get to access protected memory.\n\nValidating RsvdZ seems a good idea. I added validation for reserved fields.",
